  "result": "`ArrayBuffer.prototype.maxByteLength` is implemented in its file; all 20 test262 runs under `built-ins/ArrayBuffer/prototype/maxByteLength/` pass, and clippy is clean for the file. Only that file is changed.\n\n- **Step 3 (IsSharedArrayBuffer):** The check is always false in this engine. The only `[[ArrayBufferData]]` constructor (`allocate_array_buffer`, `kahvi-core` `object/typed_array.rs`) sets no shared flag, and the `SharedArrayBuffer` constructor is a not-implemented stub. The comment above the step points to both facts.\n- **Step 6 `None` branch:** Removed. The getter matches on the buffer's data, so the invented TypeError is gone. The fixed-length fallback reads the byte length, which step 2 guarantees exists.\n\nI dropped the `is_fixed_length_array_buffer` call in favour of that match, so the helper is no longer used here. The docs suggest `unreachable!`/`expect` for engine-bug cases, but this ticket forbids panics, so I avoided that path.\n\nBLOCKED: none",
